    "text": "<p>Antiferromagnetism, type of magnetism in solids&nbsp;in which adjacent ions that behave as tiny magnets</p><p>Paramagnetism&nbsp;is a form of magnetism whereby some materials are weakly attracted by an externally applied magnetic field, and form internal, induced magnetic fields in the direction of the applied magnetic field.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MnO</mi></math>- Antiferromagnetism<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>- Paramagnetism<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>- Diamagnetism<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>- Ferrimagnetism</p>",
